  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array AAA of size NNN, we define f(A)f(A)f(A) as follows:\n\n\nIf AAA contains NNN distinct elements, f(A)=0f(A) = 0f(A)=0.\nOtherwise, f(A)=min⁡(j−i)f(A) = \\min (j - i)f(A)=min(j−i) among all pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) satisfying 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i &lt; j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N and Ai=AjA_i = A_jAi​=Aj​.\nYou are given 222 integers NNN and KKK.\n\nYour task is to find the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all arrays AAA of size NNN satisfying 1≤Ai≤K1 \\le A_i \\le K1≤Ai​≤K. Since the answer may be large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all arrays AAA of size NNN and 1≤Ai≤K1 \\le A_i \\le K1≤Ai​≤K modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,K≤2⋅1051 \\le N, K \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N,K≤2⋅105",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of KKK over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
